From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:27:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] build(engine): verify servers against the system certificate
 store

Motivation: reqwest's rustls-tls feature verifies Google's certificates
against webpki-roots, a copy of Mozilla's list compiled into the program.
Distributions keep that list in one place (ca-certificates) and update it
with the system, administrators add their own authorities there, and a
compiled copy only changes when DriveSync is rebuilt.

Changes: rustls-tls-native-roots instead of rustls-tls; rustls-native-certs
reads the operating system's store. The Flatpak runtime ships the same
store at /etc/ssl/certs. No other behaviour changes: rustls, the ring
provider, no proxy and no redirects stay as they were.

Validation: the installed package trusts a test authority added with
update-ca-certificates and reaches a local stand-in of Google's endpoints;
the unchanged build refuses the same certificate (UnknownIssuer).

Limitations: Cargo.lock gains rustls-native-certs, openssl-probe and their
macOS and Windows dependencies (schannel, security-framework), which cargo
vendors but never builds on Linux.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (branch order299 of the edition's DriveSync fork)
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
